Z||000000||fierosound||01-25-2000||11:46 PM||||Anyone using the Sears Diehard Security Battery?   It has a remote control security system built in.  Basically, when "armed" enough power will be allowed through the electrical system to keep power to all your accessories (clocks, ECM, dome lights etc), but will not allow the car to be started until reset with the remote control.  When armed, the car can't be started by boosting, push starting, or even with the key!    Complete details below:<P> <A HREF="http://biz.yahoo.com/prnews/991201/il_sears_n_1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://biz.yahoo.com/prnews/991201/il_sears_n_1.html</A> <P>I may have a closer look at this when I need a new battery.  Wish I had one BOTH times my car was stolen before...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||14
